# Match Existing Conventions

Before writing code in any component (`snapping_etl`, `gee_etl`, `dhs_etl`,
`ml_pipeline`, `preprocessing`, `commons`), check how the **sibling components**
already solve the same problem and follow that. Do not introduce a parallel
idiom when an established one exists — consistency across components outranks
personal preference.

When adding a new function, file, or pattern, grep the repo for the same task
first (filename parsing, logging, config, file IO, caching, docstrings) and copy
the existing approach.

## Known conventions (extend as discovered)

- **Filename from a URL/path**: `Path(url).name` — not `url.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]`
  or `os.path.basename(...)`. (See `dhs_etl/extract/extractor.py`.)
- **Docstrings / comments**: single backticks `` `like_this` `` — never RST
  double backticks ``` ``like_this`` ```.
- **Logging**: root logger (`logging.info(...)`), f-strings, no per-module
  `logger` object. (See `.cursor/rules/logging.mdc`.)
- **Config**: frozen `@dataclass` `Config` + `CONFIG` singleton, env overrides,
  `pathlib.Path`. (Mirror `config_gee.py` / `config_snapping.py`.)
- **Timestamped files**: `commons.file_utils.make_timestamped_path` /
  `find_latest_timestamped_file`, UTC stamps.

## Examples

```python
# BAD — new idiom not used elsewhere in the repo
dest = dest_dir / url.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]

# GOOD — matches dhs_etl/extract/extractor.py
dest = dest_dir / Path(url).name
```
